(>> 3.1 Principles of Responsive Web Design \(RWD\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Responsive Web Design \(coined by Ethan Marcotte in 2010\) ensures web applications) Tj
T*
(automatically adapt their layout, navigation, typography, and imagery to deliver optimal) Tj
T*
(viewing experiences across any display viewport \(smartphones, tablets, laptops, 4K) Tj
T*
(monitors\):) Tj
T*
(* The 3 Cardinal Pillars of RWD:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Fluid Grids: Designing layouts using relative percentage \(%\) or fractional \(fr\)) Tj
T*
(units rather than rigid absolute pixels \(px\).) Tj
T*
(- 2. Flexible Media: Ensuring images and video scale dynamically within parent bounds:) Tj
T*
(img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }.) Tj
T*
(- 3. CSS Media Queries: Applying conditional style sheets based on device display) Tj
T*
(characteristics \(viewport width, orientation, resolution\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.2 Viewport Configuration and CSS Media Queries) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* The Essential Viewport Meta Tag: Placed in document <head>: <meta name='viewport') Tj
T*
(content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0'>. Instructs mobile browsers to render) Tj
T*
(the document at native device pixel width rather than defaulting to a zoomed-out) Tj
T*
(980px desktop canvas.) Tj
T*
(* Media Query Syntax: @media screen and \(min-width: 768px\) { ... }.) Tj
T*
(* Mobile-First vs Desktop-First Paradigms:) Tj
T*
(- Mobile-First \(Industry Standard\): Write base CSS for mobile viewports without media) Tj
T*
(queries, then use min-width queries to progressively enhance the experience as screens) Tj
T*
(expand \(min-width: 576px, 768px, 992px, 1200px\). Reduces mobile bandwidth and CPU) Tj
T*
(overhead.) Tj
T*
(- Desktop-First: Write desktop CSS and use max-width queries to override and collapse) Tj
T*
(features on smaller screens.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.3 Relative Units: Rem, Em, %, VW and VH) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* px: Absolute pixel measurement; rigid, ignores user accessibility browser font) Tj
T*
(scaling.) Tj
T*
(* rem \(Root Em\): Relative to the font-size of the root <html> element \(default 1rem =) Tj
T*
(16px\). Changing root font-size scales the entire UI proportionately, supporting) Tj
T*
(universal accessibility.) Tj
T*
